  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` cite is correctly placed on the explicit function `fingerprint` in `impl[GraphWithChangingEdges/NodeContents]`. The commentary is in fenced citation commentary, so it counts as a tracked justification. It gives a substantive reason. `NodeContents` requires the method, but the test asserts selection-only dependencies, and a content fingerprint would contradict that. The explanation agrees with the current source:\n- The enclosing test `agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets` asserts that the only recorded dependency is `Dependency::OutgoingEdges(1, (), edge_fingerprint(&graph, &[2]))`.\n- `edge_fingerprint` in `crates/habeas-sdk/src/graph.rs` hashes node paths from `node_path` and never calls `fingerprint`.\n- `dependencies_are_current` in the same file calls `fingerprint` only for `Dependency::Node`, so an edge-only record never reaches it.\n- The sibling stubs `node_content` and `format_node_content` panic for the same reason, which fits the claim that no content is read.\n\nThe method is not meant to run and has no coverage, which the commentary accounts for. The item carries no `{impl}` or `{test}` reference to `habeas:coverage`, so the citation is not redundant. I found no gap.",
